## Interlude / Side B — English Translation (Chapters 9–12)

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 9 — Joy That Pierces the Chest
################################################################################

translate en b09_001:
    "That afternoon, the sky over the Gema Masa alley was solid gray, like a canvas soaked in spilled paint. The drizzle kept steadily dampening the asphalt. Kai stood frozen in front of the wooden shop door — his hand already halfway up to grab the handle — when the door suddenly swung open from the inside."

translate en b09_002:
    "A young woman stumbled out, her steps unsteady, like the ground beneath her had just turned into clouds. Her shoulders shook violently. She was sobbing, clutching a cassette tight against her chest — as if that plastic shell were her own heart starting to beat again."

translate en b09_003:
    kai "{i}(jumps back, stepping aside){/i} Uh— go ahead, Mbak..."

translate en b09_004:
    "Kai braced himself to see a face full of grief — an expression he figured would feel all too familiar with his own fate. Yet as she passed him, what he saw was completely different: behind the spilling tears, she was smiling. Radiant. Pure. As if this narrow alley had suddenly gained a second sun."

translate en b09_005:
    wanita "{i}(whispers softly, as if talking to herself){/i} They're real, Mas... Really there. I heard them. Crying... so loud."

translate en b09_006:
    "She kept walking, still sobbing, still smiling. Through the door that hadn't quite swung shut, Kai caught sight of Pak Ageng standing behind the counter, watching her back — silent, with the knowing glint in his eyes of someone who already understood everything."

translate en b09_007:
    kai_hati "She just listened to a tape. And she's crying... out of happiness. Both at the same time. How is that even possible?"

translate en b09_008:
    "Later on, Kai learned the woman's story. For years, she had waited for a miracle that never came. She'd nearly given up on her quiet womb."

translate en b09_008_p2:
    "Then, in this shop — through a cassette paid for at a price only she and Pak Ageng knew — she heard a sound from the future: a baby's first cry. Her baby. Just a few months away."

translate en b09_009:
    kai_hati "She heard the sound of a life just about to begin. The most beautiful song she'd ever heard, she said. And me? I heard... nothing. Silence. Complete silence. Which my brain translated straight into: the end."

translate en b09_010:
    kai_hati "Same shop. Same sixty-second tape. Heaven for her, hell for me. {i}(pause){/i} The contrast... it really stings. How can somebody else's happiness feel like a knife to the chest?"

translate en b09_011:
    "Kai didn't go inside after all. He couldn't face Pak Ageng's calm this afternoon. He turned around and walked straight back into the thickening rain."

translate en b09_012:
    "At home, the living room was warm and lively. Mom and Dad were laughing at something on TV. The smell of dinner still hung in the air. A completely ordinary scene — and tonight, it felt a million miles away from Kai."

translate en b09_013a:
    ibu "Oh, Kai, you're back. Your clothes are soaked through. Go eat first. This show is hilarious — your Dad almost—"

translate en b09_014a:
    ayah "{i}(laughs){/i} Almost choked on a cracker. No need to finish that story."

translate en b09_015a:
    "Kai sat on the edge of the sofa. He laughed along — quiet, half a beat behind everyone else, but a laugh all the same. Mom slid a plate of food over without asking too many questions."

translate en b09_016a:
    kai_hati "Laughing. It's so easy for them. {i}(pause){/i} For me... it should be easy too. It should be."

translate en b09_013b:
    "From the doorway, Kai lifted his phone. One photo: Mom and Dad laughing, candid, completely unaware they were being photographed."

translate en b09_014b:
    kai_hati "Just in case. If on Friday I... {i}(shakes his head quickly){/i} If I don't get to see something like this again, at least there's proof. That a night like this actually happened."

translate en b09_013c:
    ibu "{i}(from the living room){/i} Kai? Are you home? Come eat first, honey—"

translate en b09_014c:
    kai "{i}(calling back){/i} Already ate, Bu. I'm full. Just gonna rest."

translate en b09_015c:
    "A lie. His stomach had been empty since noon. Still, his feet had already carried him into his room before anyone could stop him."

translate en b09_017:
    "His bedroom was spotless. Way too neat for a seventeen-year-old: books lined up, desk wiped clean — and sitting on top of the desk, a white envelope sealed shut. Kai sank onto his bedroom floor, leaning back, staring up at the ceiling with tired eyes."

translate en b09_018a:
    "He opened his phone gallery. The photo of the evening sky from a few days ago was still there — orange, calm, completely clueless about Friday."

translate en b09_019a:
    kai_hati "The sky's still the same. I'm the only one who changed."

translate en b09_018b:
    "From the desk drawer, he pulled out his small notebook and flipped to the page he'd written a few days ago. His own handwriting, just a short line."

translate en b09_019b:
    kai_hati "\"I'm still here today.\" {i}(pause){/i} ...Yeah. Today, I still am."

translate en b09_018c:
    "No photo. No note. A clean desk, a head empty of good things. Kai stared at the ceiling, trying to summon even one good memory from this week — and all that came back was the silence from that tape."

translate en b09_019c:
    kai_hati "Empty. Just like my tape."

translate en b09_020:
    "He pictured the baby's cry that woman had heard — loud, alive, just beginning. Then he compared it to the silence on his own tape. Suddenly, that silence felt way louder than any scream."

translate en b09_021:
    kai_hati "Friday. Four in the afternoon. {i}(swallows hard){/i} Giant footsteps. Slow, but unstoppable. Coming straight to crush me."


################################################################################
## CHAPTER 10 — Escape to a Quiet Room
################################################################################

translate en b10_001a:
    kai_hati "Mom and Dad's laughter from last night is still echoing in my head. Warm. ...And then I remember what day it is."

translate en b10_001b:
    kai_hati "Last night's photo is still open on my phone. Mom, Dad, laughing. ...And then I remember what day it is."

translate en b10_001c:
    kai_hati "Quiet. From last night straight through waking up, nothing but quiet. ...And today's Friday."

translate en b10_002:
    "The very first thing Kai felt upon waking was his own heartbeat — hammering hard against his ribs, his breathing ragged. His hand pressed over his chest. Still beating. He glanced at his desk: the digital clock glowed red. 5:00 AM. The sun hadn't even chased the night away yet."

translate en b10_003:
    kai "{i}(whispers){/i} ...Alive. I'm still alive."

translate en b10_004:
    "The relief lasted all of three seconds. Because Kai knew the exact hour of the \"event\" on the tape: 4:00 PM. Eleven hours still stretched ahead of him — like walking down death row."

translate en b10_005:
    "That morning, Kai dragged himself to school on heavy feet. In the hallways, in class, his eyes stayed blank. His body sat at his desk, while his mind already stood on the edge of a cliff. His classmates' laughter, scraping chairs, chalk scratching the board — it all blurred into a buzz of bees in his ears."

translate en b10_006:
    teman "Kai, are you okay? You look super pale, lho."

translate en b10_007:
    kai "...I'm fine. Just didn't sleep much."

translate en b10_008:
    teman "Oh. Okay then, make sure you get some rest. {i}(walks off){/i}"

translate en b10_009:
    kai_hati "The later it gets, the messier my head feels. The scenarios keep looping: if it's really today, it'll be somewhere crowded. A pileup on a busy road. The gym roof caving in. Danger can come from any direction when there are people everywhere."

translate en b10_010:
    kai_hati "I don't want my death to be a spectacle. If I really have to go today... I want to disappear quietly."

translate en b10_011:
    "The dismissal bell rang. Skipping club activities today — Kai had already made up his mind. He walked fast along the sidewalk, his eyes scanning every passing car, every power pole that looked even slightly shaky. He needed one place: lowest possible risk, no hazardous objects, no crowds."

translate en b10_012a:
    kai_hati "The City Library. Old building. Dead quiet in the afternoons — kids our age would rather hang out at cafes or the mall. No traffic, no crowds. That's the spot."

translate en b10_013a:
    "He headed straight there without looking back."

translate en b10_012b:
    "Kai lay down on a bed in the school nurse's office, claiming he felt dizzy. The first ten minutes were peaceful. Then two loud kids from the next class barged in, the nurse kept walking back and forth, the bell rang, laughter echoed down the hall."

translate en b10_013b:
    kai_hati "Can't stay here. Too many people. Too much noise. If something happens... everybody's gonna see."

translate en b10_014b:
    "He excused himself, saying he felt better — then walked briskly to the one place that had been sitting in the back of his mind: the City Library."

translate en b10_012c:
    "The school rooftop was deserted. The wind whipped past. The city stretched out below — and Kai's brain immediately filled it in with every awful way to fall."

translate en b10_013c:
    kai_hati "...Wide open. High up. Windy. Idiot. This isn't a hiding spot. It's an invitation."

translate en b10_014c:
    "He hurried back downstairs, breathing short and shallow, then walked fast toward the City Library."

translate en b10_015:
    "Kai pushed open the library's glass door. Cool air smelling of worn paper and fine dust greeted him. It was so hushed inside, like time itself moved slower here."

translate en b10_016:
    "He made his way down the aisles between towering teak bookshelves that nearly brushed the ceiling. He kept going until he reached the most tucked-away corner of the whole building: behind a row of encyclopedias nobody ever touched."

translate en b10_017a:
    "On his way to that corner, something near the big glass window at the far end caught his eye: a wooden chair — and beside it, an open gear bag resting neatly on the floor. As if someone had already claimed that spot."

translate en b10_018a:
    kai_hati "Someone else is here...? {i}(shakes his head){/i} Whatever. As long as they stay away from my corner, none of my business."

translate en b10_019:
    "There, Kai curled up on a wooden chair. Far from the window, far from any shelf that might topple onto him, far from every bad possibility. He locked his eyes onto his wristwatch."

translate en b10_020:
    kai_hati "3:30. {i}(swallows hard){/i} Thirty minutes left. Thirty minutes until total silence. ...Okay. Here I am. Safest place I could think of. If it's really coming — let it come."


################################################################################
## CHAPTER 11 — The Falling Echo That Silences
################################################################################

translate en b11_001:
    "The library's old wooden floorboards creaked softly every time Kai shifted, as if protesting his movement. Between the thick, dusty rows of encyclopedias, time felt like thick syrup — refusing to flow. The chilly air and smell of aging paper wrapped around him, offering a flimsy illusion of safety from the outside world he saw as a minefield."

translate en b11_002:
    kai_hati "3:50. Ten minutes left. {i}(presses his phone's power button one more time — the screen stays black){/i} Completely off. No buzzing, no sudden chimes. Just me and the clock."

translate en b11_003:
    kai_hati "In my head, I've already said goodbye to everything. Over and over. {i}(pause){/i} Funny thing is, the stuff I regret most is the small stuff. That white envelope — a ridiculous farewell letter I wrote myself. Seventeen years old, writing a will. If anyone found out, I'd never live it down for the rest of my life. ...Assuming I have any life left, that is."

translate en b11_004:
    "Movement at the end of the aisle caught his eye. A few meters from where he sat, a girl about his age stood in a very strange pose."

translate en b11_005:
    "She wore bulky headphones covering her ears. In her hands, she held a long pole with a fuzzy microphone at the tip — a boom mic — carefully aimed at the huge glass window at the far end of the room."

translate en b11_005_p2:
    "The glass was vibrating hard: outside, a massive truck had just rolled by, leaving a low rumble that shook the old building's foundation."

translate en b11_006:
    "She didn't look scared at all. If anything, she looked completely locked in — like she was hunting down something priceless inside the trembling glass."

translate en b11_007a:
    kai_hati "...That chair by the window. The gear bag I saw earlier. It's hers. She's been here this whole time — just like me, \"hiding out\" in the library. Difference is, she doesn't look scared at all."

translate en b11_008:
    kai_hati "Who is she? Here I am counting down my final seconds, and she's totally absorbed in her own little world — surrounded by recording gear. {i}(pause){/i} People really can be night and day, huh."

translate en b11_009:
    "Kai's watch hit 4:00 PM. On the dot."

translate en b11_010:
    kai_hati "This is it. {i}(squeezes his eyes shut; grips the edges of his chair until his knuckles turn white){/i} Goodbye. Good—"

translate en b11_011:
    "Kai jolted hard in his chair. His eyes flew open — and he could still see the afternoon sunlight slanting through the gaps between shelves. Could still feel the cool air. His heart pounded so hard his ears rang. Beating. Still beating."

translate en b11_012:
    kai "{i}(whispers, trembling){/i} ...I can still... still see. Still breathe. I'm still—"

translate en b11_013:
    "Right in front of him, a stack of thick books lay scattered across the floor. It must have tumbled off the table beside him — shaken loose by the truck's rumble, or bumped by accident. And right behind the fallen pile stood the girl with the boom mic."

translate en b11_014:
    "She froze. Her hands still gripped the microphone pole, yet her clear eyes were locked straight onto Kai. Time felt like it truly stopped turning. Fine specks of dust floated in the golden-orange light slipping between the shelves — a scene that almost didn't feel real."

translate en b11_015:
    "Kai opened his mouth. He wanted to ask if she was okay. Wanted to make any sound at all, just to prove he was still breathing. Not a single word came out. His throat had locked up — not from fear, but from something far stronger."

translate en b11_016:
    kai_hati "She's not saying anything. I'm not saying anything. Not a single sound. {i}(long pause){/i} ...Sixty seconds. This. This is it. The silence on my Friday tape — it's this. Not because I died."

translate en b11_016_p2:
    kai_hati "Not because the world went empty. Because I'm... speechless. Completely awestruck. Someone like her, standing there in the afternoon light, living at her own slow, calm tempo — and my brain completely stopped."

translate en b11_017:
    kai_hati "I'm still alive. I'm actually, really still alive."

translate en b11_018:
    "Suddenly, laughter burst straight out of Kai's chest. At first just a stifled chuckle. Then it snowballed into full-on hysterical laughter filling the quiet room. He laughed out of pure relief. Laughed at how ridiculous he'd been — drafting goodbye letters for something that turned out to be a meeting."

translate en b11_019:
    gadis "Hey! Are you crazy?!"

translate en b11_020:
    "Kai's laughter died instantly. The girl was glaring at him now, brows knitted, face flushed with annoyance. She'd already pulled her headphones down around her neck."

translate en b11_021:
    gadis "You ruined everything! I waited hours to record the sound of \"falling dust\" after a truck rumble, and you just start cackling like a lunatic! {i}(glares){/i} And you were staring at me so weirdly just now. What, are you trying to rob me or something?"

translate en b11_022:
    "Kai went silent. His face instantly turned bright red too. He looked down at the scattered books, then back at the girl — who was now roughly shoving her gear away."

translate en b11_023:
    kai_hati "Say something. Say literally anything, Kai. Before she leaves and you never see her again—"

translate en b11_024:
    kai "{i}(blurts it out, working up his nerve){/i} My name's Kai."

translate en b11_025:
    "She paused for half a second. Glanced back over her shoulder, a sharp edge still in her eyes."

translate en b11_026:
    gadis "I didn't ask for your name, Boy Waiting to Die."

translate en b11_027:
    "She slung her gear bag over her shoulder and walked off — leaving Kai stunned, and somehow feeling... alive."

translate en b11_028:
    kai_hati "\"Boy Waiting to Die.\" {i}(pauses; then cracks a small smile to himself){/i} Worst nickname I've ever gotten. And somehow... I want to hear her talk again."

translate en b11_029:
    "Outside the library, the afternoon sun was starting to fade. Yet for Kai, this Friday had only just begun — in the most unexpected way imaginable. Fate hadn't handed him death. Fate had handed him a brand-new voice, one that had never been on his tape at all."

translate en b11_030:
    kai_hati "The tape didn't lie. Sixty seconds of silence, four o'clock, Friday — all of it was true. It was just the meaning... {i}(shakes his head, smiling){/i} I read the meaning completely wrong. Way off."


################################################################################
## CHAPTER 12 — Sweetness Between Realities
################################################################################

translate en b12_001:
    "Stepping out of the library, Kai's stomach growled. Made sense — he'd been way too busy being terrified of dying all day to remember to eat. At a little canteen near the library that was about to close, he bought a drink and something to fill his stomach."

translate en b12_002a:
    "Right next to him, the canteen lady's big pot simmered quietly. The lid rattled lightly every time a bubble rose. Strangely, the sound was soothing. Today's sound. The sound of right now."

translate en b12_003a:
    kai_hati "Boiling. Noisy — yet alive. {i}(smiles faintly){/i} Actually pretty nice to listen to, huh."

translate en b12_002b:
    "Kai sat in the quietest corner, far from everyone else. Old habit. He ate slowly while looking down at his own hands — hands that could still hold a spoon after all."

translate en b12_003b:
    kai_hati "Still able to eat. Still able to sit in a canteen. Little things like this... turns out they're a luxury."

translate en b12_002c:
    "Kai ate standing outside the canteen, facing the street. Motorbikes rolled past, people walked by, life kept moving — all completely normal, clueless that a few minutes ago some kid had thought his life was ending at four this afternoon."

translate en b12_003c:
    kai_hati "The world didn't stop back there. Only I did. ...And now it's moving again."

translate en b12_004:
    "Kai's steps felt heavy as he headed back down that ever-wet dead-end alley. His face still burned — the blush on his cheeks refused to fade even in the cool afternoon air. The lingering embarrassment of laughing hysterically in front of that girl, plus his ridiculous goodbye letter, still bruised his pride."

translate en b12_005:
    "The bell above Gema Masa's door chimed. Pak Ageng didn't even need to look up to know who had walked in — he could already tell from the way the door opened: a little hesitant, yet with leftover sparks of energy behind it. The old man was arranging a few bite-sized snacks on a small ceramic plate."

translate en b12_006:
    ageng "{i}(calm tone, with a hint of amusement){/i} Back so soon, kid?"

translate en b12_007:
    "Kai didn't answer right away. He dropped onto the wooden stool at the counter and buried his face against the cool teak tabletop."

translate en b12_008:
    kai "{i}(muffled against the table){/i} You knew, didn't you? You definitely knew that silence wasn't because I died."

translate en b12_009:
    "Pak Ageng chuckled — his laugh sounded like the soft rustle of an old cassette tape: warm, and full of memories. He slid the ceramic plate across to Kai."

translate en b12_009_p2:
    "Arranged on it were colorful pieces of cenil — pink, green, and white — dusted with fresh grated coconut and drizzled with thick palm sugar syrup. A tiny fork rested beside the plate."

translate en b12_010:
    ageng "I told you — these tapes never lie, but human ears mishear things all the time."

translate en b12_011:
    "Kai slowly lifted his head. His eyes lingered on the cenil glistening under the shop's warm yellow light."

translate en b12_012:
    ageng "The cassette records what's going to happen, Kai. It never gets the frequency wrong. What gets it wrong is how your heart translates those sounds."

translate en b12_013:
    "Pak Ageng gazed toward the shop window, where a few raindrops still clung to the glass. His eyes drifted far away, as if looking past the walls of this dead-end alley."

translate en b12_014:
    ageng "{i}(whispers softly){/i} Sometimes, silence is louder than a shout. There are moments when every sound around you suddenly drops away — not because your world stopped, but because your heart is being made to listen to something louder than words."

translate en b12_015:
    "Kai picked up a piece of cenil and popped it into his mouth. Chewy, mixing with the savory coconut and sweet palm sugar. The sweetness seemed to slowly wash away the embarrassment and leftover fear still sitting in his chest."

translate en b12_015_p2:
    "He pictured the girl's face in the library again — and that falling stack of books, ringing out like a bell announcing his life had just started all over again."

translate en b12_016:
    kai "That kind of silence... it really made my chest feel tight, Pak."

translate en b12_017:
    ageng "{i}(smiles faintly){/i} That's just how it feels when you're completely awestruck, Kai. It's the most honest kind of silence there is. No tricks, no pretending. Just you and whatever's standing right in front of you."

translate en b12_018:
    ageng "{i}(teasing){/i} So, what's your plan for tomorrow? Still wanna buy another cassette?"

translate en b12_019:
    kai "{i}(slowly shakes his head, finishing the last piece of cenil){/i} Not for now, Pak. I think... I want to try listening to today's sounds first."

translate en b12_020:
    ageng "{i}(nods approvingly){/i} Wise choice. Because the tapes on these shelves aren't running off anywhere — whereas a moment like the one at the library might never repeat itself the same way."

translate en b12_021:
    "Kai stared at the rows of cassettes for a long moment. For the first time, those shelves didn't look like the answer to anything. Just shelves. And that felt... light."

translate en b12_022:
    kai_hati "Just today for now. Today's sounds. {i}(pause){/i} ...What's her name, anyway? I didn't even get a chance to ask. All I know is the nickname she slapped on me. {i}(smiles){/i} That's fine. I'll figure it out someday soon."
